UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Our world needs graduates who thrive in an era of uncertainty and change. In the Monash Bachelor of Arts you will cultivate your intellect, foster your passions and develop your capacity to ask the questions and find the solutions required to transform our world.</p> <p>The Monash Bachelor of Arts is designed to give you maximum flexibility and choice. You can choose from over thirty areas of study to build a genuinely transformative experience. The course is built around deeply enriching experiences, including local and international internships, professional engagements and entrepreneurial opportunities, and the choice of over fifty global immersion programs. You will build a unique graduate profile, preparing you to live and work in complex and culturally diverse environments. You may like to continue on in your learning journey and complete honours or postgraduate study.</p> <p>The Bachelor of Arts has four <a href="https://www.monash.edu/arts/professional-futures">Professional Futures</a> domains which build skills and abilities that employers value and seek. You will not be required to do any single specific unit across these domains. Instead, you can build your own suite of experiences and attributes to create a graduate profile that is unique to you:</p> <p><strong>Global Immersion</strong></p> <p>Broaden your knowledge and life experience by participating in the <a href="https://www.monash.edu/global-immersion-guarantee">Global Immersion Guarantee</a> or one of our other short study trips or a semester-long programs. Our high quality international mobility experiences help our graduates to engage in the world and prepare them for the global workplace.</p> <p><strong>Intercultural Expertise</strong></p> <p>Build skills to thrive in globalised work places and communities. The reality for all our graduates is that they are competing in a global employment market and whether they find themselves in local, national or international organisations these will all be multi-cultural environments. The capacity to successfully navigate the complexities of culturally different environments is a signature capability of an Arts graduate. These units are designed to specifically address the development of our students’ capabilities.</p> <p><strong>Professional Experience </strong></p> <p>Through industry internships and placements, create networks and skills for your career development. Professional experiences allow you to start activating your knowledge in real world scenarios. It aids you to see your learning in an employment context.</p> <p><strong>Innovation Capability</strong></p> <p>Cultivate an innovation mindset as you develop your creative and enterprising abilities. These units offer you the opportunity to understand and build innovation capabilities and enterprising skills. You are challenged to seek/build the solutions required to transform our world by leveraging your own experiences and activities outside the classroom.</p><h4>Structure</h4><p>The course is structured in three parts: Part A. Major studies, Part B. Specified studies and Part C. Free elective studies.</p> <p><strong>Part A. Major studies</strong><br/><br/>These units will provide you with a focused program of study that will develop your practical and theoretical skills and knowledge in one Faculty of Arts listed major area of study. You will learn to critically analyse, apply and communicate an advanced level of understanding of the concepts and theoretical frameworks that constitute the knowledge base of the area of study.</p> <p><strong>Part B. Specified studies</strong><br/><br/>These units will expose you to several arts disciplines contributing breadth to your knowledge of the arts, humanities and social sciences. You will have the flexibility of learning about several areas of study before finalising your choice of major. You will also build skills and abilities that employers value and seek by completing units from the Professional Futures domains. <br/><br/><strong>Part C. Free elective studies</strong></p> <p>These units will enable you to further develop your knowledge of your chosen major, or to investigate other areas of interest. You may choose electives from units offered within the Bachelor of Arts or any other Arts undergraduate course, or you can explore different disciplines and experiences offered from across Monash. This includes taking undergraduate units offered by other Faculties, and/or participating in University programs such as <a href="https://www.monash.edu/flagship-rich-experiences/home">Flagship Rich Educational Experiences</a> (FREE).</p> <p><strong>Bachelor + Master''s accelerated pathway</strong></p> <p>If you satisfy the below requirements, you may be invited to join the bachelor + master''s accelerated pathway:</p> <ul><li>have achieved a minimum Weighted Average Mark (WAM) of 65%; and </li><li>have completed a minimum of 96 credit points in your bachelor''s degree, including 24 credit points towards your Arts major.</li></ul> <p>Please note that you should also have a minimum of 24 credit points of free electives available.</p> <p>On joining the accelerated pathway your 24 credit points of free elective units will be replaced with specified units from your destination master''s degree. As long as you attain a minimum WAM of 60% at the end of your bachelor studies, you will be eligible to continue your chosen master''s degree the following year/intake.</p> <p><strong>Course progression map</strong></p> <p>The <a href="https://www.monash.edu/arts/course-information/maps/">course progression map</a> provides guidance on unit enrolment for each semester of study.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4><p>Monash College - Diploma of Arts<br/>Monash Access Program<br/>Monash Transition Program<br/>Arts (Indigenous Entry)<br/>Articulation agreement: Beijing Foreign Studies University (1+3) Exp: 19-May-24 *Renewal in progress<br/>Articulation agreement: Beijing Foreign Studies University (2+2) Exp: 19-May-24 *Renewal in progress<br/>Articulation agreement: Beijing Institute of Technology (2+2) Exp: 19-May-24 *Renewal in progress<br/>Articulation agreement: Henan University (2+2) Exp: 17-Apr-24 *Renewal in progress<br/>Articulation agreement: Beijing Normal University (2+2) Exp: 10-May-23 *Renewal in progress</p><h4>English Language Requirements</h4><p>Monash Level A, that is: IELTS (Academic): 6.5 overall (no band lower than 6.0); or Pearson Test of English (Academic): score of 58 overall with no band lower than 50; or TOEFL Internet-based test: score of 79 overall with minimum scores: Writing: 21, Listening: 12, Reading: 13 and Speaking: 18; or Equivalent approved English test</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.monash.edu/2026/courses/A2000',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '075404D';

