UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>The Bachelor of Business will enable you to delve into the dynamic world of business. You will have the opportunity to understand what makes organisations, brands and markets function effectively and sustainably. Whether you are interested in working for a large corporation, or a not-for-profit organisation, managing a business, or becoming an entrepreneur, the Bachelor of Business will give you the knowledge and skills you need to thrive in a competitive business landscape. The course provides choice and flexibility by allowing you to develop broad business knowledge as well as specialised expertise in one or two chosen areas of business practice. It also offers you the opportunity to study overseas or undertake an internship, as well as a range of other experiences which enable you to maximise your employability at graduation. <br/><br/>You will be well equipped to seek employment in both private and public-sector enterprises.</p><h4>Structure</h4><p>This is a comprehensive course, structured in four parts: <br/><br/><strong>Part A. Core studies</strong><br/><br/>These studies will provide you with a broad foundation for your study of business and expose you to several business disciplines. It will contribute breadth to your knowledge of business and develop your understanding of multi-disciplinary decision making in organisations. It will also give you the opportunity to learn more about each discipline before finalising your choice of major. <br/><br/><strong>Part B. Major studies</strong><br/><br/>Your major studies will provide you with a focused program of study that will develop your expertise. You will develop, apply and communicate an advanced level of understanding of the concepts and theoretical frameworks that constitute the knowledge base of your major area of study.</p> <p><strong>Part C. Capstone studies</strong></p> <p>This is designed to consolidate the knowledge and skills acquired throughout the study of your major.</p> <p><strong>Part D. Elective studies</strong><br/><br/>This will enable you to further develop knowledge of your chosen major, or business more broadly, or study a second business major. Alternatively you can select units from across the University in which you are eligible to enrol.</p> <p><strong>Masters Accelerated Pathway</strong></p> <p>The Bachelor of Business offers an <a href="https://www.monash.edu/business/current-students/course-advice-and-planning#Accelerated_pathways-7">Accelerated Pathway option</a> into the Master of Business, Master of Global Business, Master of Management, Master of Applied Marketing and Master of Regulation and Compliance. This Accelerated Pathway allows you to complete a master’s degree with one additional year of full-time study.</p> <p>If you have completed at least 96 credit points and have achieved a high credit (65%) average, you can apply to the Course Director for the master’s accelerated pathway. If admitted to the accelerated pathway, you will use four units (24 credit points) of your elective studies (Part D) to complete master-level units from one of the destination courses.</p> <p>Note: You still need to meet the entry requirement of having an overall 65% weighted average mark at the end of your degree to enter the master’s program.</p> <p><strong>Course progression map</strong></p> <p>The <a href="https://www.monash.edu/business/current-students/course-advice-and-planning/helpful-links/course-maps/2026/undergraduate">course progression map</a> provides guidance on unit enrolment for each semester of study.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4><p>Diploma of Tertiary Studies - Business<br/>Diploma of Higher Education - Business<br/>Monash Transition Program<br/>Monash College - Diploma of Business<br/>Monash College - Diploma of Commerce<br/>Business (Indigenous Entry)</p> <p><strong>Articulation agreements:</strong></p> <p>Abu Dhabi University - 2.5+1.5 - Exp: 12/07/2025<br/>Amity University (Noida campus) - 2+2, (1.5+1.5), (1+2) - Exp: 01/07/2025<br/>Beijing Foreign Studies University (BFSU) - 2+2 - Exp: 19/05/2024 renewal in progress<br/>Beijing Institute of Technology, Zhuhai (BITZH) - 2+2 - Exp: 19/05/2024 renewal in progress<br/>Beijing Jiaotong University (BJTU) - 2+2 - Approval in progress<br/>Central South University (CSU) - 2+2 - Exp: 25/11/2025<br/>Central University of Finance and Economics (CUFE) - 2+2 - Exp: 16/06/2024 renewal in progress<br/>Diplomatic Academy of Vietnam (DAV) - 1+2 - Exp: 27/06/2027<br/>Dongbei University of Finance and Economics (DUFE) - 2+2 - Exp: 11/11/2024<br/>FPT Education Global - 2+2 - Exp: 02/06/2026<br/>Guangdong University of Finance (GDUF) - 2+2 - Exp: 12/12/2024 renewal in progress<br/>Guangdong University of Technology (GDUT) - 2 + 2 - Exp: 16/04/2028<br/>Hanoi University of Science and Technology (HUST) - 2.5+1.5 - Exp: 07/08/2026<br/>Henan University - 2+2 - Exp: 17/04/24 renewal in progress<br/>Hunan University - 2+2 - Exp: 19/07/2026<br/>International University, Vietnam National University (IU VNU HCMC) - 1.5+1.5 - Exp: 12/12/2026<br/>Jiangnan University (JNU) - (3+1) &amp; (3+1.5) - Exp: 24/05/2025<br/>Narsee Monjee Institute of Management Studies (NMIMS) - 1.5 + 1.5 - Exp: 05/09/28<br/>O.P Jindal Global University - 1.5+1.5 - Exp: 16/05/2027<br/>Shanghai International Studies University (SISU) - 1.5+2 - Exp: 13/01/2027<br/>Shanghai University of Finance and Economics (SUFE) - 1.5+2 - Exp: 30/09/2026<br/>South China Agricultural University (SCAU) - 2+2 - Exp: 23/05/2027<br/>Southwestern University of Finance and Economics (SWUFE) - 2+2 - Exp: 28/02/2027<br/>University of Danang (DUE - UE) - 2+2 - Exp: 12/02/2028<br/>University of Danang (DUE - VNUK) - 2+2 - Exp: 17/08/2025<br/>University of Economics and Business, Vietnam National University (UEB-VNU) - 2+2 - Exp: 29/08/28<br/>University of Economics, International School of Business, Ho Chi Minh City (UEH-ISB) - (1.5+1.5) &amp; (1+2) - Exp: 29/11/2027<br/>Vidyalankar School of Information Technology (VSIT) - (1.5+2), (2+1.5), (2+2) - Exp: 31/01/2026<br/>Xi''an International Studies University (XISU) - 2 + 2 - Exp: 30/05/2029<br/>Xi''an Jiaotong-Liverpool University (XJTLU) - 2 + 2 - Exp: 30/06/2029<br/>Zhengzhou University (ZZU) - 2+2 - Exp: 25/07/2026</p><h4>English Language Requirements</h4><p>Monash Level A, that is: IELTS (Academic): 6.5 overall (no band lower than 6.0); or Pearson Test of English (Academic): score of 58 overall with no band lower than 50; or TOEFL Internet-based test: score of 79 overall with minimum scores: Writing: 21, Listening: 12, Reading: 13 and Speaking: 18; or Equivalent approved English test</p>',
