UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>The Diploma of Engineering will prepare you for success in your Monash Engineering degree.</p> <p>In the first year of this course you will learn about the maths and science theory and skills you will need for University. In the second year, you will study the same subjects as first-year University students and develop your specialist knowledge of engineering and the practical skills you will need for University. Students will be able to select from one of the following specialisations: </p> <ul> <li>Aerospace Engineering</li> <li>Biomedical Engineering</li> <li>Chemical Engineering </li> <li>Civil Engineering </li> <li>Electrical and Computer Systems Engineering </li> <li>Environmental Engineering</li> <li>Materials Engineering</li> <li>Mechanical Engineering</li> <li>Robotics and Mechatronics Engineering </li> <li>Software Engineering</li> </ul><h4>Structure</h4><p>This course is structured in two parts Part 1. Foundation knowledge and Part 2. Discipline knowledge.</p> <p><strong>Part 1. Foundation knowledge</strong></p> <p>These units will provide you with the foundational maths and science theory and practical skills you’ll need for University and to progress to your discipline studies.<br/><br/><strong>Part 2. Discipline knowledge</strong></p> <p>These units are equivalent to first-year University units and will provide you with discipline specific knowledge in engineering to enable progression to your destination bachelor degree.</p>',
