UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>The Doctor of Philosophy (Clinical Psychology) is a professional doctorate program that integrates advanced practitioner training in clinical psychology with graduate research training to prepare you for work as a Clinical Psychologist and an academic leader in the field of clinical psychology. Our graduates use their knowledge of psychology and mental health for the assessment, diagnosis, formulation, treatment and prevention of psychological problems and mental illness across the lifespan in research and clinical settings. </p> <p>The course is founded on a commitment to excellence in clinical training and clinical research that can positively impact the brain and mental health of the community. During the program, you will conduct an independent, meaningful and novel investigation of a research problem relevant to clinical psychology under the guidance of experienced academics. You will learn from passionate clinical educators through coursework, and expert clinical supervisors across three clinical placements. You will become a scientist-practitioner with generalised and specialised clinical skills, that enables you to respond to complex mental health problems, that is culturally responsive, in order to help people thrive.</p> <p>The course is accredited by the Australian Psychology Accreditation Council (APAC) as a fifth and sixth year of study in Psychology. Graduates of the program are eligible for general registration as a Psychologist and entry to a registrar program toward Area of Practice Endorsement as a Clinical Psychologist.</p><h4>Structure</h4><p>This course consists of coursework (10 percent), practicum placements (20 percent), and doctoral research (70 percent). The first two years must be undertaken full-time. From third year, domestic students may elect to complete their studies on either a full-time or part-time basis.</p> <p><strong>Research and thesis </strong></p> <p>You must, in consultation with and under the direct supervision of a member/s of the academic staff:</p> <ol><li>carry out a program of research on an agreed topic approved by the faculty in the psychology discipline for a specified period, including attending and/or presenting at seminars and other related activities as indicated by the faculty</li><li>submit for assessment a thesis of not more than 80,000 words on the program of research which meets the requirements of the examiners. The thesis should embody the results of the student''s investigation, which demonstrates independence of thought and the student''s ability to carry out research in psychology. Submission of a <a href="https://www.monash.edu/graduate-research/supervisors-and-examiners/examiners/publication">thesis including published works</a> may be permitted.</li><li>satisfactorily complete the required coursework units and placements.</li></ol> <p><strong>Coursework</strong></p> <p>Coursework is conducted during the first three years of the course. Learning objectives will be predominantly assessed through competency-based assessment tasks that reflect professional skills, knowledge and attitudes.</p> <p>While much of the teaching will take place at Monash University''s Clayton campus and the Turner Clinics in Notting Hill, students should be prepared for some travel to other locations.</p> <p><strong>Placement</strong></p> <p>These opportunities will enable you to apply theory to practice under the supervision of experienced clinical supervisors. You will complete a minimum of 1000 hours of professional experience, with 400 hours of direct client contact, across three different hospital or community settings.</p> <p><strong>Year 1</strong></p> <p><strong><em>Full Year</em></strong></p> <p><a href="https://handbook.monash.edu/2024/units/PSY6210?year=2024">PSY6210 Research Methods</a></p> <p><strong><em>Semester 1</em></strong></p> <p><a href="https://handbook.monash.edu/2023/units/PSY6102">PSY6102 Psychological Assessment</a></p> <p><a href="https://handbook.monash.edu/2023/units/PSY6103">PSY6103 Ethical, Legal and Professional Practice</a></p> <p><a href="https://handbook.monash.edu/2023/units/PSY6104">PSY6104 Cognitive and Behaviour Therapies: Processes and Applications A</a></p> <p><a href="https://handbook.monash.edu/2023/units/PSY6101">PSY6106 Psychopathology A</a></p> <p><strong><em>Semester 2</em></strong></p> <p><a href="https://handbook.monash.edu/2023/units/PSY6105">PSY6105 Clinical Developmental Psychology</a></p> <p><a href="https://handbook.monash.edu/2024/units/PSY6107">PSY6107 Psychopathology B</a></p> <p><a href="https://handbook.monash.edu/2024/units/PSY6109">PSY6109 Cognitive and Behaviour Therapies: Processes and Applications B</a></p> <p><strong>Year 2</strong></p> <p><strong><em>Full Year</em></strong></p> <p><a href="https://handbook.monash.edu/2023/units/PSY6205">PSY6205 Introductory Placement and Case Analysis</a></p> <p><strong><em>Semester 1</em></strong></p> <p><a href="https://handbook.monash.edu/2023/units/PSY6207">PSY6207 Health Psychology and Behavioural Medicine</a></p> <p><strong>Year 3</strong></p> <p><strong><em>Semester 1</em></strong></p> <p><a href="https://handbook.monash.edu/2023/units/PSY6206">PSY6206 Intermediate Placement and Case Analysis</a></p> <p><strong><em>Semester 2</em></strong></p> <p><a href="https://handbook.monash.edu/2023/units/PSY6204">PSY6204</a><a href="https://handbook.monash.edu/2023/units/PSY6204"> Advanced Clinical Practice</a></p> <p><a href="https://handbook.monash.edu/2023/units/PSY6301">PSY6301 Advanced Placement and Case Analysis</a></p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 208,
    offshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>English Language Requirements</h4><p>Monash Level D: IELTS (Academic): 7.0 overall (no band lower than 7.0); or Pearson Test of English (Academic): score of 65 overall with no band lower than 65; or TOEFL Internet-based test: score 98 overall with minimum scores: Writing: 27, Listening: 24, Reading: 24 and Speaking: 23; or Equivalent approved English test.</p> <p>Please note: as students need to be provisionally or generally registered as a psychologist on commencement of the course, you must also be able to meet the mandatory <a href="https://www.psychologyboard.gov.au/documents/default.aspx?record=WD15%2f16880&amp;dbid=AP&amp;chksum=px4gMFl360IujXiFqasp3g%3d%3d">AHPRA English language skills registration standard</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.monash.edu/2026/courses/4585',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '095943M';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>You will undertake your doctoral studies through the <a href="http://www.monash.edu/migr/future-students/phd">Monash doctoral program</a>. At the core of this program is the completion of a substantial research thesis on an agreed topic under the guidance of a supervisory team. Your research training is further enhanced by professional development activities designed to support you in your academic and professional development.</p> <p>Upon completion of your doctoral studies at Monash, you will be able to demonstrate that you have successfully designed and executed a research project that makes an original and substantial contribution to your discipline. In your research journey, you will have also acquired the necessary skills and professional attributes to make an immediate and enduring impact on academia, industry, government, or community.</p><h4>Structure</h4><p><strong>This course consists of:</strong></p> <ul><li>a research and thesis component</li><li>a creative work component</li></ul> <p>You must satisfy the following requirements in consultation with and under the direct supervision of a member/s of the academic staff:</p> <ol><li>carry out a program of research approved by the program of enrolment, including attending and/or presenting at seminars and other related activities as indicated by the program of enrolment.</li><li>submit for assessment a thesis which meets the requirements of the degree. There are two components to this thesis, and they need to have a clear focus on education. </li></ol> <p>The first component consists of an original substantive creative work/collation of artifacts that relates explicitly to a learning context of your choosing. This work could consist of one of the following three options and must be relevant to the particular education-focused program of research:</p> <ol><li>A written creative work of around 35,000 words. This work can be multimodal, and may include creative writing in the form of stories, plays, poems, a short book or a portfolio of writing in different genres.</li><li>A substantive digital creative work/collation of works. This may include musical performance or film production of 70-90 minutes in duration (in total if this is a collation of works), or a cohesive portfolio of work hosted on a website. In all cases, it needs to demonstrate significant involvement and effort. </li><li>A collection of visual artifacts. This work will consist of a portfolio of original artwork that can be examined by exhibition.</li></ol> <p>The second component is an accompanying critical component of around 35,000 words (or equivalent) that can take the form of an exegesis, a work of scholarly research or a combination of both:</p> <ul><li>a scholarly exegesis which comments directly on the creative work in terms of its theoretical framing and educational potential.</li><li>an independent but complementary work of scholarly research on a topic relevant to the research objectives of the creative work.</li></ul> <p>The total thesis component must not exceed 80,000 words (or equivalent).</p> <p>Submission of a <a href="https://www.monash.edu/graduate-research/supervisors-and-examiners/examiners/publication">thesis including published works</a> may be permitted.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 208,
    offshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td>As per Monash PhD handbook English language proficiency requirements.</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.monash.edu/2026/courses/D8001',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '117340H';

