UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>There has never been a more important or exciting time to study the mediated world.</p> <p>This course builds your understanding of the changing contexts of media and communication practices. You will gain insight into the key issues affecting the communications and media industries and you will examine these developments from cultural, political and theoretical perspectives.</p> <p>This course develops an understanding of the contemporary communications and media environment. It is suitable to those pursuing careers in a wide range of communications and media roles, including in the areas of communications, media relations, social media, digital engagement, public policy and public relations.</p><h4>Structure</h4><p>The course comprises 24 credit points of study which provide knowledge, skills, attitudes and values required of skilled practitioners working in a range of fields addressing communications and media studies.</p> <p><strong>Course Progression map</strong></p> <p>The <a href="https://www.monash.edu/arts/course-information/maps">course progression map</a> provides guidance on unit enrolment for each semester of study.</p>',
