    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>The Graduate Certificate of Corporate and Financial Regulation is designed to advance lawyers’ and non-lawyers’ skills and knowledge of developments in the principles, practice, and scholarship of corporate and financial regulation. You will receive a theoretical and practical grounding in corporate and financial regulation.</p> <p>This course provides you with the corporate and financial regulation knowledge that will give you a competitive edge in a career in corporate and financial regulation.</p><h4>Structure</h4><p>The course consists of four units or 24 credit points of study. You can choose units from a selected list of Monash Law''s postgraduate electives to gain the Corporate and financial regulation knowledge that will give you a competitive edge in your chosen career.</p> <p><strong>Course progression map</strong></p> <p>The <a href="https://www.monash.edu/students/handbooks/maps/2026/map-l4008.pdf">course progression map</a> provides guidance on unit enrolment.</p>',
