UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>The Master of Design is a dynamic and forward-thinking program tailored for the rapidly evolving field of design. This course equips you with the skills and knowledge required to excel and lead in various design disciplines. You will delve into advanced principles of contemporary design, refine your design practice, and graduate with an industry-relevant qualification that positions you at the forefront of the profession.</p> <p>At Monash University, we cultivate designers who are independent, inquisitive, and socially responsible. Our graduates emerge as vital contributors and potential leaders in sustainable design, addressing issues ranging from climate action to social and cultural equity. The Master of Design offers three specialisations:</p> <ul> <li>Interaction Design</li> <li>Multimedia Design</li> <li>Design Research</li> </ul> <p>These specialisations prepare graduates to play crucial roles in various domains of design, fostering innovative solutions and leadership. You can personalise your learning experience by selecting a specific design specialisation or opting for the Design Research specialisation. This specialisation allows you to concentrate on a design research project within any field of design, such as industrial, spatial, collaborative, communication, and motion design.</p> <p>The program is structured around four core design studio units, spread across four semesters. These studios include both defined and self-directed design projects that span design systems, services, processes, environments, and artefacts. Through these projects, you will demonstrate high-level planning, resource management, implementation, and evaluation, leading to a thorough understanding of professional design processes.</p> <p>In addition to the core studios and research units, you will complete three elective units that enhance your skills and knowledge in relevant disciplines. These electives are designed to complement and extend your core studies, providing a well-rounded education in design.</p> <p>The Master of Design offers an enriching educational journey that prepares you to become a leading design professional. With a strong focus on advanced design principles, research, and industry relevance, this course empowers you to make a meaningful impact in the world of design.</p><h4>Structure</h4><p>The course is structured in four parts: Part A Foundation studies (24 credit points), Part B. Studio practices (42 credit points), Part C. Critical contexts (12 credit points) and Part D. Discipline electives (18 credit points).</p> <p><strong>Part A. Foundation studies</strong><br/>These studies provide you with the conceptual thinking and technical skill set required for advanced postgraduate study in this area.</p> <p><strong>Part B. Studio practices and Part C. Critical Contexts</strong><br/>In your studio practice units you will focus on the application of advanced design problem solving skills at a professional level. You will consolidate skills and practice of design research methodologies and may extend your research trajectory to further study.</p> <p>Your critical context studies will support your research and practice and formalise your research skills.</p> <p>You will focus on the application of conceptual thinking and technical skills to advanced design problem solving. You will analyse and create a project outcome based on research, critique, and the application of design processes appropriate to your specialisation.</p> <p>In the final semester you will pursue a major design project or participate in a leading industry project. You will bring together your advanced technical ability, conceptual thinking, entrepreneurial studies and design management in practice.</p> <p><strong>Part D. Discipline electives</strong><br/>These elective studies provide you with the opportunity to deepen and broaden your knowledge and practice through the selection of electives and allow you to build capabilities in your chosen area.</p> <p><strong>Master''s entry points</strong></p> <p>Depending on prior qualifications you may receive entry level credit (a form of block credit) which determines your point of entry to the course:</p> <ul><li>If you are admitted at entry level 1 you complete 96 credit points, comprising Part A, B, C and D.</li><li>If you are admitted at entry level 2 you complete 72 credit points, comprising Part B, C and D</li><li>If you are admitted at entry level 3 you complete 48 credit points, comprising Part B (30 credit points, comprising Studio 3 and Studio 4), Part C (6 credit points, comprising TAD5500) and Part D (12 credit points).</li></ul> <p>Note: If you are eligible for credit for prior studies you may elect not to receive the credit and complete one of the higher credit-point options. <br/><br/>A zero-credit-point unit in art, design and architecture occupational health and safety (OHS1000) will also be undertaken. This unit is required of all students in the Master of Design and must be completed even if credit is obtained for Parts A or B.</p> <p><strong>Course progression map</strong></p> <p>The course progression maps provide guidance on unit enrolment for each semester of study. Please ensure that you refer to the correct course map for your semester of commencement:</p> <p><a href="https://www.monash.edu/students/handbooks/maps/2026/map-f6002.pdf">Semester 1, 2026 intake</a></p> <p><a href="https://www.monash.edu/students/handbooks/maps/2026/map-f6002-sem2.pdf">Semester 2, 2026 intake</a></p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 104,
    offshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>Monash Level A: IELTS (Academic) 6.5 overall, no band lower than 6.0</li><li>Monash Level A: Pearson Test of English (Academic) score 58 overall, no band lower than 50</li><li>Monash Level A: TOEFL iBT score 79 overall with minimum Writing 21, Listening 12, Reading 13, Speaking 18</li><li>Monash Level A: Equivalent approved English test</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.monash.edu/2026/courses/F6002',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '089737A';

