ineering, remote sensing, environmental engineering, mining and resources engineering, renewable and geothermal energy systems, computational modelling and simulation.</p> <p><strong>Electrical and computer systems engineering</strong></p> <p>Computer systems and software engineering, control engineering, electronics, telecommunications engineering, electrical power systems, bio-optics, biomedical engineering, plasmonics, nanophotonics, optical physics and robotics.</p> <p><strong>Materials science and engineering</strong></p> <p>Engineering alloys &amp; processing, additive manufacturing, phase transformations &amp; microstructure–property relationships, mechanical, corrosion &amp; behaviour modelling, advanced polymers, composites &amp; surface properties, polymer chemistry &amp; processing, biomaterials, tissue engineering, 3D bioprinting, scaffolds, drug delivery &amp; antimicrobial coatings, functional, energy, photovoltaic, 2D, magnetic &amp; spintronic materials, materials characterisation, modelling &amp; theory, advanced microscopy, synchrotron &amp; neutron methods, atomic structure analysis, computational materials science, ceramics, nanomaterials, surface/interface design, electrospun &amp; melt-spun films, aerospace &amp; defence materials, nuclear materials, sovereign capability development.</p> <p><strong>Mechanical and Aerospace engineering</strong></p> <p>Aerodynamics, fluid mechanics, turbulence, structural mechanics, aerospace engineering, composites, heat transfer, micro/nano fluid and solid mechanics, robotics, mechatronics, railway engineering and maintenance engineering.</p>',
