UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>The Master of Health Science incorporates key aspects of health science including data analysis, processing and management, within the health context. The course builds upon competency in statistical and exploratory analysis, data formats and languages, processing of massive data sets, management of data and its role and impact in health. Health topics include essential knowledge and skills in epidemiology, biostatistics, health promotion and disease prevention and application to current health care issues.</p><h4>Structure</h4><p>The course is structured into two parts: Part A. Advanced expertise and Part B. Advanced Health Science Core Studies.<br/><br/><strong>Part A. Advanced Expertise<br/></strong>These units are taken within the partner degree at Southeast University Suzhou and recorded as block credit for this course.<strong><br/><br/>Part B. Advanced Health Science Core Studies</strong></p> <p>In these studies, you will gain expertise and competence in key aspects of health science and essential knowledge and skills in epidemiology, biostatistics, health promotion and disease. These units are taken at Monash University. </p> <p><strong>Course progression map</strong></p> <p>The <a href="https://www.monash.edu/students/handbooks/maps/2026/map-m6034.pdf">course progression map</a> will provide guidance on unit enrolment for each semester of study.</p>',
